<section class="panel cp-intro cp-span-full">
    <h2>World of Warcraft: Forever — What Is It?</h2>
    <p><strong>World of Warcraft: Forever is the official Classic+ product, announced at BlizzCon 2026.</strong> It is a permanent, evergreen version of original Azeroth being built and expanded by the Classic team. Blizzard has stated plainly that it is "not a mode, a season, or a new version of Classic" — it is a third WoW experience alongside Modern and Classic, with the level cap fixed at 60 forever.</p>
    <p>Forever launches globally <strong>November 4, 2026 at 3:00 p.m. PST</strong>, with beta beginning <strong>September 17</strong>. It is included with an active subscription (game time) — no separate purchase is required to play, outside of optional pre-purchase packs. Blizzard's China-only <strong>Titan Reforged</strong> (a level-80 Vanilla/TBC/Wrath merge) had been widely read as the working prototype, and the internal project codename chased in this tracker since October 2025 was <strong>Project Camelot</strong>, tied to encrypted Patch 1.60 development builds.</p>
</section>

